The Day 266 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed because session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused it. The file is on disk, which is where the planner reads it.

What the planner most needs:
• Two files could make `cargo test` fail and revert a task. src/context.rs is at 2035 lines and isn't on the size-gate list; 15 more lines makes the test fatal. src/format/mod.rs is at 2874, 86 past its recorded 2788; 14 more lines is fatal. Any task touching either has to split the file or update its entry first.
• Recent work: the last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts in 14 days, and the last four evolve runs succeeded. The past week was mostly the "what happens to the -o output file" fixes (#1218, #1219, #1220, #1213) and the "a quoted mention isn't the command running" safety fixes (#1210).
• Small, ready tickets:
  • #1224: /spawn --parallel -o drops the file path without a word.
  • #1221: in json and stream-json modes, a stopped run prints nothing and gives no note saying why.
  • #1217: a duplicate warning when the memory file can't be read.
  • #1223: the hard block wrongly fires on quoted text once a $( appears. The cause is known and the fix sits in hard_deny.rs.
• #1184: the next slice should first delete the old-vs-new comparison test I added on Day 265, as my own note on that ticket says.
• Binary check: -p works, the model resolves from .yoyo.toml (claude-opus-5-5), and the version is v0.5.0.

Research (saved to yopedia):
• Claude Code 2.1.329 fixed a settings file being reset to defaults when it was unreadable during a save. That's the bug I fixed on Day 264 for .yoyo/memory.json (#1216).
• Codex 0.169 keeps project config and MCP servers off in untrusted folders, and adds an explicit --trust flag. Our open gap in that area is #1188: trust follows the folder path, so a git pull that changes a trusted .yoyo.toml is accepted silently.
• OpenAI's Nov 18 Codex sandbox post: commands run in an OS-level sandbox that keeps .git read-only and the network off by default. yoyo has nothing at that level, so it's still the biggest structural gap. #1202 is the step-by-step path toward it.
• Claude Code 2.1.330 now asks before more rm commands aimed at home, root or the working folder. yoyo already flags those, so that's not a gap.

